Yes, if the RNG is absolutely, positively *determined* to kill you, it
can usually find a way.

The one that annoys me the most is when the game just keeps generating
too-powerful monster after too-powerful monster, faster than you can
kill them (like, every time you and your pet manage to kill two or
three monsters, it generates four or five more, so they accumulate),
and it just *will* *not* *let* *up*, so you keep fleeing to other
levels, again and again, hoping to heal and never getting the chance,
until eventually every level you've visited has a collection of
monsters you aren't powerful enough to face, and you have like two
hitpoints and no food and are closely pursued and weak or even
fainting from hunger, and you pray and the diety is pleased but does
not fix your hunger *or* your hitpoints.

I've had this happen a number of times to my Tourist characters
(perhaps as much as 10% of the time, though that percentage is a very
rough guess as I haven't kept track of actual numbers), and also
sometimes to Wizards.  If it is avoidable, I should dearly love to be
let in on the secret technique.


